Speed up FT9366 matching: build templates on all CPUs, cache them

Every verify rebuilt each enrolled print's template from its 20 images
(20 keypoint extractions + 190 pairwise registrations, ~0.5 s per finger on
one core). Now these jobs run in parallel, built templates are cached while
fprintd runs, the probe's keypoints are extracted once per touch, and
enrollment registers each new image incrementally instead of rebuilding.
Matching results are unchanged.

